{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>In the evening, and you shall know.</b> May it be His will that what He told me — that He will give you food — will come about in this manner: that He gives you in the evening the needs of the evening, so that you know that the blessed El brought you out entirely from the land of Egypt — for He will bring you out also from its customs, that you were sitting there upon a pot of meat, without a fixed mealtime, like beasts — as they said of blessed memory: at first Israel were like chickens pecking in the dunghill, until Moses came and established for them a fixed mealtime."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Sforno reads the verse as Moses's paraphrase of his hope; the opening יְהִי רָצוֹן reflects Moses's petitionary framing rather than a direct translation of the Hebrew words."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:47.037000010Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}